# Linear identifier in commit messages

If the work being committed is from a **Linear** task (user named the issue, pasted a Linear URL, or the branch/title includes the identifier), the commit **subject** must start with that ticket identifier in square brackets.

## Format

```
[TEAM-123] Short subject focused on why
```

- Use the Linear identifier only (`ABC-123`), not the issue title and not the full `linear.app` URL.
- One pair of square brackets, immediately at the start of the subject, then a space, then the rest of the message.
- If several issues apply, use the **primary** ticket for this commit.

## Examples

```
[DAT-42] Fail closed when Basic Auth env vars are missing
[ENG-108] Quote ilike terms so topic search cannot inject filters
```

## Do not

- Invent an identifier when the work is not tied to Linear — omit the brackets entirely.
- Put the id in the body only, in parentheses, or after the subject.
- Repeat the identifier if the subject already starts with `[TEAM-123]`.
